WEBVTT

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.000
أعوذ بِٱللَّهِ مِنَ ٱلشَّيْطَـٰنِ ٱلرَّجِيمِ

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Bism Allah Arrahman Arraheem

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.000
In the name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Dr. Khalifa: This morning about 9 o'clock, Lisa asked me "do you know that you're giving the Khutba?

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.000
It was quite a surprise as you realize.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:31.000
Then after the Khutbah, Lydia came to me and said "do you know you're giving the Quranic study?"

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.000
And she took the beating on behalf of Lisa.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.000
Actually, Lisa sent her to tell me that.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.000
So, here I am.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.000
First of all, we welcome a new member to our masjid.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.000
This person here.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.000
I forgot his name.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.000
This is the former, and still is, Muhtesem Erisen, the one and only.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.000
Mã Shã Allãh

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Welcome back.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:09.000
Before I start, there is also one more point that I wanted to mention.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.000
Thanks to our Iranian brothers and sisters.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.000
There is a little bit of confusion now about your arms, what to do with your arms when you pray.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.000
Keep them like this and put them straight down.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:25.000
I would like to establish first, once and for all, that it doesn't make any difference,

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:28.000
whether you go like this or put your hands down.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:33.000
But generally, what I do is I follow what the Imam is doing.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:38.000
The person in the front, whatever the person in front is doing, I do what he's doing.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:42.000
And I recommend that for you.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:50.000
IN SHAA ALLAH, we'll be doing Sura 90, The Town.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.000
And whatever we can afterwards.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:58.000
At 8:30, the children will practice on us.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:01.000
You know, they'll be singing at the conference.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:06.000
So, we'll give them maybe 20 minutes, 20 minutes to 9.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:07.000
20 minutes enough?

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:10.000
20 minutes to practice a new song on us.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.000
It should be enjoyable, IN SHAA ALLAH.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:19.000
Sura 90, The Town.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:22.000
In the name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:26.000
[90:1] I solemnly swear by this town.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.000
[90:2] The town where you live.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.000
[90:3] The begetting and the begotten.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:38.000
[90:4] We created the human being to work hard (to redeem himself).*

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:42.000
[90:5] Does he think that no one will ever call him to account?

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:46.000
[90:6] He boasts, "I spent so much money!"

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.000
[90:7] Does he think that no one sees him?

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.000
[90:8] Did we not give him two eyes?

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:55.000
[90:9] A tongue and two lips?

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:56.000
Number 10,

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:58.000
[90:10] Did we not show him the two paths?

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.000
[90:11] He should choose the difficult path.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:05.000
[90:12] Which one is the difficult path?

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.000
[90:13] The freeing of slaves.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.000
[90:14] Feeding, during the time of hardship.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:13.000
[90:15] Orphans who are related.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:15.000
[90:16] Or the poor who is in need.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:23.000
[90:17] And being one of those who believe, and exhorting one another to be steadfast, and exhorting one another to be kind.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.000
[90:18] These have deserved happiness.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:30.000
[90:19] As for those who disbelieved in our revelations, they have incurred misery.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:34.000
[90:20] They will be confined in the Hellfire.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.000
So, that's the whole Sura.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.000
I go back to the beginning, swearing.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:47.000
God usually starts many of these short Suras with a profound statement.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:51.000
And this town, meaning Mecca, is profound.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:56.000
Because God made it sacred by putting His shrine there

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:59.000
to serve as the focal point.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:02.000
or a point of organization for all believers around the world.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:08.000
When we stand in Prayer, we don't fight as to which direction we should face.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:12.000
God already decided for us that we're gonna face the direction of Mecca.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:20.000
So, every believer, every Muslim around the world is praying and facing that point.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:26.000
So, the first verse is simply a profound statement, as in many other Suras.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:31.000
And it is the town where the Prophet Muhammad lived

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.000
from whom this Quran was revealed.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:39.000
"The begetting and the begotten" is a profound statement again.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:44.000
All these profound statements precede an important proclamation.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:54.000
The begetting and the begotten, this is a profound fact of life.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.000
Take for example birds.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.000
The bird laying an egg.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:03.000
The egg has been fertilized by two parents, through two parents.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:08.000
One half, a reproductive cell is half a normal cell.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:15.000
One reproductive cell from the male and one half, the other half comes from the female.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:17.000
They combine to form an embryo.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:21.000
In birds, the egg is laid, it is fertilized.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:32.000
And then, the fact that the birds sit on the eggs, you know they take turns, the male and female in most species.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:34.000
Taking turns sitting on the egg.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:36.000
Why do they do that?

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:38.000
Who taught them to do that?

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:42.000
And what's happening inside that shell, the egg?

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:56.000
After a period of time, that it is becoming obvious more and more that it's a multiple of 7. 21 days in some birds.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:58.000
21, 7 times 3.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:04.000
The human fetus now is in the mother's womb 266 days.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:08.000
It is now established scientifically. 266, not 265.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:12.000
266 and that's 19 times 2 times 7.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:14.000
That's still a multiple of 7.

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:20.000
Gestation period, is it called the gestation period?

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:23.000
Is that the period inside the womb?

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:30.000
Ok. In many other species, I know it is a multiple of 7, but I'm being distracted now.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.000
However, "the begetting and the begotten" is a profound statement.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:41.000
After 21 days, the bird inside breaks through the shell and comes out.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:47.000
Then, they're walking around. If they're ducks, they go in the water and they swim. You know, as if they've been here forever.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:49.000
As if they know everything.

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:53.000
Walking around, following their mother in the water.

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:58.000
You can go to a random spot and see them. They just came out of the egg.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:05.000
And they're full of wisdom, you know, just following the mother wherever she goes. And sometimes they go independently and pick at something in the water.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:09.000
And they're identical to their parents.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:14.000
With beaks and eyes. Where did this come from?

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:20.000
And you can do this with any kind of species, any begetting and begotten.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:25.000
Now here comes the proclamation. Number 4.

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:29.000
[90:4] We created the human being to work hard (to redeem himself).*

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:36.000
As a result of that crime that we committed millions of years ago,

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:40.000
where we did not make a firm stand with God's absolute authority,

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:42.000
we are here.

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:50.000
And God designed our plan to work hard, to redeem ourselves, to denounce that crime,

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:56.000
to prove that we are on the side of God's absolute authority.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:02.000
What do you call getting up in the morning before sunrise?

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:07.000
It's not easy, is it? At the beginning, especially when our soul is still small and weak.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:11.000
The soul cannot wake up the body initially.

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:14.000
Because the soul is weak.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:16.000
It is hard work.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:23.000
And you are rewarded by growth, nutrition, and strength of the soul.

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:30.000
[90:4] We created the human being to work hard.....

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:38.000
The lazy person who does not work hard and does not get up before sunrise, what is the result?

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:47.000
He or she ends up with a shrunken, weak soul that will not amount to anything in the real life, the Eternity.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:53.000
They will be born into Eternity deformed.

00:08:56.000 --> 00:09:01.000
And we see this in Sura 68 where they cannot fall prostrate.

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:06.000
On that big day when God comes physically to our universe,

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:08.000
they will not be able to, they have no legs.

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:11.000
I mean, this is symbolically. They are deformed.

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:14.000
A stump cannot fall prostrate.

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:17.000
They are deformed.

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:19.000
It is lack of growth.

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:25.000
To get up in the morning before sunrise and do the Morning Prayer is a gift from God.

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:31.000
If we deserve it, God will guide us into waking up before sunrise to do the Morning Prayer.

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:41.000
For the young people, I don't want you to be alarmed because it may be difficult for you, but eventually

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:45.000
you will be able to train your body to get up in the morning before sunrise.

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:48.000
If you are unable to do it now, don't be too disturbed.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:54.000
It is normal. Let me tell you this because I don't wanna be too hard on you.

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:58.000
It is normal to start out by doing one prayer a day.

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:03.000
Let us say the Morning Prayer as soon as you get up at 10 or 11 in the morning.

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:06.000
Then, it will be two prayers a day.

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:09.000
Then, it will be three prayers a day.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:14.000
Then, you will do the Morning Prayer before sunrise and you will enjoy it.

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:23.000
The ideal situation is to do the five Prayers with the Morning Prayer done before sunrise.

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:29.000
Also, God tells us in the Quran that we cannot do it every day. You're gonna miss once in a while.

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:36.000
So, always think of the positive and be glad, be happy with the achievements that you do.

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:41.000
If you miss one time a week or something, don't feel too guilty.

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:47.000
Be glad that you did six out of the seven days, Morning Prayers before sunrise.

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:53.000
Ideally, you will not miss anything. You will do the Morning before sunrise and you will do the other four Prayers as well.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:58.000
[90:4] We created the human being to work hard (to redeem himself).*

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:04.000
There's a footnote here that says "see the Introduction and Appendix 7 for the purpose behind our creation.

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:07.000
Redeem ourselves.

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:09.000
Go back to God's kingdom where we were.

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:20.000
We got ourselves out by being interested in Satan's theory that others besides God can have power.

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:24.000
And the people are doing the same mistake now.

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:32.000
They think Jesus can have power, or Mary, or Saint Jude, or Muhammad, or Ali, or Hussein, or Mahdi, or whatever.

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:35.000
People are repeating the same mistake.

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:38.000
We did. God saved us.

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:41.000
This is how we get redeemed.

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:47.000
By upholding the words of God alone and worshipping God alone.

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:53.000
Number five talks about those who fail to redeem themselves.

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:57.000
[90:5] Does he think that no one will ever call him to account?

00:11:58.000 --> 00:12:06.000
See, everything we do here is credited to us or held against us, whatever we do here.

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:15.000
And anything is forgivable except idol worship

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:17.000
if maintained until death.

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:23.000
That's the unforgivable crime, because this is why we are here.

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:30.000
We are here for just one reason, to establish the fact that we know that only God possesses all power.

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:37.000
And so number five is telling us that every one of us will be called to account.

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:43.000
With the majority of people, they'll be asked "why didn't you develop your soul?

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:48.000
How come you fed your body three meals a day, but you failed to feed yourself, your soul?"

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:57.000
Most people go through their whole life without feeding the real person a single meal.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.000
This is repeated in the Quran.

00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:05.000
Most people, no matter what you do, will not believe.

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:11.000
And most of those who believe will fall into idolatry, into idol worship.

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:14.000
And we see this everywhere, don't we?

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:21.000
Just think of any mosque in the world that says the Adhan, for example, the call to prayer, devoted to God alone,

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:25.000
without the name of Muhammad or Ali or somebody besides God.

00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:33.000
In all of Iran or Pakistan or Egypt or Saudi Arabia, there isn't a single one mosque

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:37.000
that is devoted to God alone, which goes against the commandments of the Quran.

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:41.000
What happened to their brains?

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:46.000
They're just repeating what they did in the High Society.

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:55.000
[90:5] Does he think that no one will ever call him to account?

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:58.000
[90:6] He boasts, "I spent so much money!"

00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:00.000
Isn't this what most people do?

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:05.000
They're preoccupied with the almighty dollar.

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:14.000
In the meeting with our brothers and sisters in New York, I was asking them

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:18.000
"when you get up in the morning, what is your list of priorities?"

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:22.000
"Are you going to have three meals today?"

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:28.000
Just when you open your eyes in the morning, ask yourself these questions.

00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:30.000
"What am I gonna do today? I'm gonna have three meals today?"

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:34.000
That's about 30 minutes, at least.

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:36.000
"Am I going to the bathroom today?"

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:38.000
Two or three times.

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:42.000
"Am I going to work today?"

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:44.000
Four to eight hours.

00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:48.000
"Am I going to exercise today?"

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:50.000
Thirty to sixty minutes.

00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:54.000
"What else will I do? Will I watch the TV today for one or two hours?"

00:14:56.000 --> 00:15:00.000
"Will I give God twenty-five minutes? Will I do my five Prayers today?"

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:08.000
Even with some Muslims, the five Prayers take a back seat to everything else.

00:15:09.000 --> 00:15:11.000
You ask them "why don't you come to the Friday prayer?"

00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:15.000
"Why don't you do the five Prayers?"

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:20.000
They will say "I had an appointment here and there, and I did this and that, and there was no time for the Prayer."

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:31.000
But we thank God because all of us here, we work our schedules around the Prayers, the five Prayers.

00:15:31.000 --> 00:15:33.000
That's the proper thing to do.

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:40.000
It should be that when we get up in the morning, on top of the list will be the five Prayers, at least.

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:43.000
On top of the list.

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:47.000
Then, if there is time for anything else, we will do that.

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:53.000
This is why the verse that says "most of those who believe, fall in idol worship."

00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:58.000
Because when you give priority to anything else, that's your idol.

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:04.000
Now, don't get me wrong. There are situations where you are forced by circumstances to miss

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:08.000
a Prayer or two, or a Friday, an occasional Friday.

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:10.000
And I don't want you to feel guilty about that either.

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:16.000
Because God Himself in the Quran gives you, knows what's in your heart, and gives you excuses.

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:21.000
But generally in your life, you're giving priority to God and your duties towards God,

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:24.000
which are actually a gift from God to you.

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:28.000
So, when you get up in the morning, you think, I'm gonna have three meals today.

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:34.000
I'm gonna give my body at least a half hour for eating.

00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:37.000
Eating, drinking, snacking, more.

00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:39.000
You're really taking care of your body.

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:42.000
How about your soul?

00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:47.000
The believers have their priorities in the right order.

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:53.000
When I open up my eyes in the morning, the five Prayers, this will take precedence over everything else.

00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:00.000
Number six,

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:02.000
[90:6] He boasts, "I spent so much money!"

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:08.000
Because they're devoted to that. Money is the god of most people, unfortunately.

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:17.000
If the boss says "you're gonna come tomorrow at three o'clock in the morning", they will set the alarm at two o'clock.

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:23.000
They will get up at two o'clock, very energetic, put on their clothes and go

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:26.000
to that field trip at three o'clock in the morning.

00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:34.000
Yet, their job or their boss does not give them that money. It is God who is giving them the money.

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:43.000
I want to share with you an important verse, so I go get my index.

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:51.000
Speaking of money, in verse six, it's a very important verse that we should all be very familiar with.

00:17:55.000 --> 00:18:01.000
I think it is in Sura 29, I'm not sure, but I will give you the correct Sura and verse right now.

00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:17.000
Yeah, it is Sura 29, verse 17.

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:24.000
Let me have the whole Quran.

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:26.000
Lydia, are you gonna read it for us?

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:29.000
Dr. Khalifa: 29:17.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:44.000
Lydia: [29:17] "What you idolize besides GOD are idols from your creation; you." Whatever idols you set up possess no provisions for you. Therefore, seek provisions only from GOD. Worship Him alone, and be appreciative of Him; to Him will be your return.

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:47.000
Dr. Khalifa: It's a very important verse you must all remember, 29:17.

00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:53.000
It says "the idols you set up besides God", and it appears here that specifically the

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:58.000
money idol, the almighty dollar, do not possess the power to provide for you.

00:18:58.000 --> 00:19:03.000
Therefore, seek provisions from God, because God is the Only Provider.

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:06.000
And as believers we know that. We must believe that.

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:08.000
No one else is the provider.

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:15.000
Many of you have gone through this experience and they know that the people who interview

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:18.000
you and give you jobs and so on, they have no power whatsoever.

00:19:19.000 --> 00:19:21.000
God is the One who's running them.

00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:31.000
This is why verse 7, verse 6 illustrates the stupidity of most humans.

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:33.000
[90:6] He boasts, "I spent so much money!"

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:36.000
Or I made so much money, you know, same thing.

00:19:38.000 --> 00:19:43.000
